From a2fb73ff2f17fe1f390186ef1ee74f7d07a5f07a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baily <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:53:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): add observer lifecycle hook events
 (PermissionRequest, Stop, SessionEnd)

Extends the hooks system beyond SessionStart with three fire-and-forget
observer events:

- PermissionRequest: a turn settled on a tool call awaiting approval
- Stop: a turn settled back to idle (status: ok | error)
- SessionEnd: the CLI session is shutting down

Observer hooks are executed for their side effects only: stdout is
ignored (logged at debug level), failures are logged without affecting
the main flow, and dispatches are never awaited by the running turn.
Settle detection mirrors TerminalProgressService.trackStream exactly and
lives in a new HookLifecycleService wired at the same stream boundaries
in the TUI and headless run controllers; SessionEnd fires from async
disposal during DI container shutdown.

Config loading reuses the existing user/project merge (project hooks
stay disabled by default), timeout handling, and sensitive env var
stripping.

Related to #2684

Signed-off-by: Baily <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
